# Per-file line-count ceilings for scripts/check_line_limits.sh.
#
# Format: <path><TAB><ceiling><TAB><note>. Blank lines and lines starting
# with `#` are ignored; the path is root-relative and matched exactly. A
# listed file is still reported when it is over its path-picked cap, but
# only fails the run when it exceeds the ceiling here.
#
# Ceilings are the file's measured line count and only ratchet down: when a
# listed file shrinks, lower its ceiling to the new count, and delete the
# entry once the file is back under its cap. When a listed file grows past
# its ceiling the gate is red by design — trim the file rather than raising
# the number.
#
# Counts measured after the 80-column reflow (Item 1.11).
